@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Filter regression harness
+
+`filter_test.c` includes the production filter with the registration object
+disabled. It uses real OBS headers and deque code, with deterministic stand-ins
+for resampling and model calls. It checks both callback orders, missing-reference
+timeout, bounded reference retention, concurrent context retirement, and failed
+reload preservation. It does not open OBS or audio devices.
+
+On the Windows MinGW toolchain used for this review:
+
+```powershell
+$env:PATH = 'E:\msys64\ucrt64\bin;' + $env:PATH
+gcc -std=gnu11 -O2 -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections `
+  -I E:/obs-studio-32.2.2/libobs -I E:/LocalVQE/ggml `
+  obs-plugin/tests/filter_test.c '-Wl,--gc-sections' -pthread -o filter_test.exe
+./filter_test.exe
+```
+
+The sidechain now has a bounded two-hop (32 ms) matching window. Output reserves
+three hops including model framing (48 ms at 16 kHz), so callback order does not
+starve the reference. This adds 32 ms relative to the previous one-hop padding.
